  <!-- EN: A huge herbivorous mammal with a temperamental disposition. Black rhinos differ from their white relatives in their slightly smaller size and in lip shape. The black rhino has a pointed upper lip, while whites have a squared lip, a difference related to the animals' diets: Black rhinos are browsers that get most of their sustenance from eating from bushes.\n\n<color=#33d733>Real World Conservation Status:</color> Critically endangered. Three of the seven subspecies of black rhino have become extinct since 1850  and one is on the brink of extinction. As of 2020, thanks to the persistent efforts of conservation programmes across Africa, black rhino numbers have risen to a current population of between 5,366 and 5,627 individuals. -->
